# Milestone: M6 (revised at v0.9.1)
# Covers: Phase 2 atom-method dispatch — slot lookup starting from a
# non-UVAL_OBJECT receiver routes through the realm-global atom proto
# (Integer / String / etc.).
#
# v0.9.1 spec §4.2 froze every builtin atom proto, so the pre-v0.9.1
# style `Integer.marker = 42; 1.marker` no longer compiles — script-side
# slot install on a builtin proto raises TypeError.  We verify the same
# routing path here via the existing C-native method surface that's
# installed during stdlib boot (Integer.asString, Float.asString,
# String.length).  These methods reach the literal receiver via the
# identical urbi_atom_proto_for_value lookup the pre-v0.9.1 user-slot
# fixture exercised.

# Integer literal dispatches through the Integer atom proto.
1.asString()
[00000000] "1"

99.asString()
[00000001] "99"

# Float literal dispatches through the Float atom proto (Gap #5 closed
# at v0.6.2: 3.14 parses as a single FLOAT token).
3.14.asString()
[00000002] "3.14"

# String literal dispatches through the String atom proto.
"hello".length()
[00000003] 5
